Galaxy S9+ Exynos integration and publication

This publication builds on Scion-Project's fork of HakiOS and the upstream
components identified in SOURCES.md. Original source notices and licenses are
retained under core/. Kernel-derived code remains under its applicable APSL
and component licenses; MIT does not relicense third-party material.

The installed GLES release and Metal/Vulkan work in progress are separate.
No affiliation with Apple, Samsung, Scion-Project, UniXNU, Mesa or Project
Silicium is asserted. Their names identify the original work and hardware.

No Apple SYSTEM image, Apple restore archive, personal partition backup,
Wi-Fi password, saved network profile, personal MAC or SSH private key is included.
The BOOT template clears the original MAC slot; installers supply their own
device identity locally without publishing it.

Release BOOT prefixes contain the hardware support/firmware already required
by the tested Scion device image. Preserve the device/firmware and UEFI
attribution and qualifications in core/NOTICE and SOURCES.md.

Galaxy A50 (Exynos 9610) port

The Galaxy A50 work (core/devices/a50, the Exynos 9610 parts of core/drivers and
core/xnu/patches/1520-a50-exynos9610.patch, core/tools/a50-fvp.py) is by nespaces,
built on the Galaxy S9+ publication by danstronics and on HakiOS/Scion-Project.
It includes no Samsung firmware and no Apple software: the builder supplies both
from their own phone and IPSW.
